 RemoveAllComments←{
⍝ Removes all lines that start with a lamp (`⍝`) -- except inside code blocks and <pre> blocks.
⍝ Code blocks are detected by `WhereAreCodeBlocks`, the same way as everywhere else, so a fence
⍝ with an info string (like `~~~ apl`) is recognized as well.
     ns←⍵
     md←ns.markdown
     isCode←WhereAreCodeBlocks md
     preStart←(≢md)⍴0
     preStart[1+'<pre\b'⎕S 2⊢md]←1
     preEnd←(≢md)⍴0
     preEnd[1+'</pre>'⎕S 2⊢md]←1
     isPre←Between(~isCode)∧preStart≠preEnd     ⍝ A line holding both opens and closes a block
     keep←isCode∨isPre∨'⍝'≠⊃¨md
     ns.markdown←keep/md
     ns.lineNumbers←keep/ns.lineNumbers
     ns
 }
